\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces A walking family of triangles ($N=3$). Ring $n$ has inradius $ns+\varphi $, its centre $c_n = \mathbf  {R}_{n\theta }(n\delta )$ walks along the dotted spiral, and its own frame is turned by $n\theta $. Rendering asks for the distance from $p$ to the nearest ring; the residual of ring $n$ is measured in that ring's frame, on the pulled-back point $q_n = \mathbf  {R}_{-n\theta }\,p - n\delta $. Because each ring has a different frame, no single scalar field of $p$ has these rings as its level sets.\relax }}{11}{figure.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:family}{{5}{11}{A walking family of triangles ($N=3$). Ring $n$ has inradius $ns+\varphi $, its centre $c_n = \Rot {n\theta }(n\delta )$ walks along the dotted spiral, and its own frame is turned by $n\theta $. Rendering asks for the distance from $p$ to the nearest ring; the residual of ring $n$ is measured in that ring's frame, on the pulled-back point $q_n = \Rot {-n\theta }\,p - n\delta $. Because each ring has a different frame, no single scalar field of $p$ has these rings as its level sets.\relax }{figure.caption.28}{}}
